        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/valor-mortis-header_J59Ly2I.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Valor Mortis plays a bit of a sneaky trick. For a while it keeps it straight. 'Yes', it seems to say; 'I'm definitely a Soulslike. Look at my bonfire equivalents, my healing flasks, my corpse runs, even my early impossi-boss feints. Look at my cautious action, my fog gates, the oppressive air of melancholy that lingers over these fields of mud and blood'. But jumpcut to a few hours later, and there you are: first-person wall-running, grapple-swinging, one-two parry slashing, quick-step-fire-ball-dismembering, slow-mo bullettime high-jump shotgun-blast-to-the-face-ing. This, it's fair to say, is not your usual Soulslike.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/valor-mortis-review\">Read more</a></p>",
